    {
      "id": "2528dc17dfd9aba929eefa50d14f8a1ee32f1764",
      "type": "paper",
      "title": "OCSCNet-Tracker: Hyperspectral Video Tracker Based on Octave Convolution and Spatial–Spectral Capsule Network",
      "abstract": "In the field of hyperspectral video tracking (HVT), occclusion poses a challenging issue without a satisfactory solution. To address this challenge, the current study explores the application of capsule networks in HVT and proposes an approach based on octave convolution and a spatial–spectral capsule network (OCSCNet). Specifically, the spatial–spectral octave convolution module is designed to learn features from hyperspectral images by integrating spatial and spectral information. Hence, unlike traditional convolution, which is limited to learning spatial features, the proposed strategy also focuses on learning and modeling the spectral features. The proposed spatial–spectral capsule network integrates spectral information to distinguish among underlying capsule categories based on their spectral similarity. The approach enhances separability and establishes relationships between different components and targets at various scales. Finally, a confidence threshold judgment module utilizes the information from the initial and adjacent frames for relocating the lost target. Experiments conducted on the HOT2023 dataset illustrate that the proposed model outperforms state-of-the-art methods, achieving a success rate of 65.2% and a precision of 89.3%. In addition, extensive experimental results and visualizations further demonstrate the effectiveness and interpretability of the proposed OCSCNet.",
      "year": 2025,
      "venue": "Remote Sensing",
      "url": "https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/2528dc17dfd9aba929eefa50d14f8a1ee32f1764",
      "citation_count": 0,
      "reference_count": 43,
      "fields_of_study": "",
      "is_open_access": true,
      "tldr": "This study explores the application of capsule networks in HVT and proposes an approach based on octave convolution and a spatial–spectral capsule network (OCSCNet), designed to learn features from hyperspectral images by integrating spatial and spectral information.",
